  </div>\n   297→                    <div class=\"item-date\">Released: 2025-08-25</div>\n   298→                    <div class=\"community-quote\">\n   299→                        \"Currently no other solution is performing as good as QODER! I have done several A/B testings with Python and JS projects. Also in larger NextJS projects the overall outcome beats currently all others\"\n   300→                    </div>\n   301→                </div>\n   302→            </section>\n   303→\n   304→            <!-- Whitelist Updates Section -->\n   305→            <section class=\"whitelist-updates\">\n   306→                <h2>📈 Product Updates</h2>\n   307→\n   308→                <div class=\"item\">\n   309→                    <div class=\"item-title\">GitHub Copilot</div>\n   310→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   311→                        <strong>Copilot memory and JetBrains features</strong><br>\n   312→                        New Copilot memory features and Ollama integration in GitHub Copilot for JetBrains. Copilot Memory helps the assistant become more effective by remembering facts about repositories and personal coding preferences across workflows.\n   313→                    </div>\n   314→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   315→                        <span class=\"tag\">feature</span>\n   316→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-11</span>\n   317→                    </div>\n   318→                    <div class=\"item-link\">\n   319→                        <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/concepts/agents/copilot-memory\" target=\"_blank\">View Details →</a>\n   320→                    </div>\n   321→                    <div class=\"community-quote\">\n   322→                        \"GitHub Copilot now remembers what it learns across your workflow. Copilot coding agent, CLI, and code review share knowledge automatically.\"\n   323→                    </div>\n   324→                </div>\n   325→\n   326→                <div class=\"item\">\n   327→                    <div class=\"item-title\">Claude Code</div>\n   328→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   329→                        <strong>Cross-session messaging</strong><br>\n   330→                        Claude Code sessions can now message each other on macOS and Linux, enabling Claude to pass findings and decisions between sessions instead of requiring re-explanation. Introduces ListAgents and SendMessage tools for coordinating work across terminals and worktrees.\n   331→                    </div>\n   332→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   333→                        <span class=\"tag\">feature</span>\n   334→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-03</span>\n   335→                    </div>\n   336→                    <div class=\"item-link\">\n   337→                        <a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/whats-new\" target=\"_blank\">View Details →</a>\n   338→                    </div>\n   339→                    <div class=\"community-quote\">\n   340→                        \"463 upvotes on Reddit with users praising it as cool and useful for avoiding repeated context explanations\"\n   341→                    </div>\n   342→                </div>\n   343→\n   344→                <div class=\"item\">\n   345→                    <div class=\"item-title\">Claude Code</div>\n   346→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   347→                        <strong>Self-hosted environments in public beta</strong><br>\n   348→                        Self-hosted environments run Claude Code cloud sessions on infrastructure your organization operates, now in public beta on Team and Enterprise plans.\n   349→                    </div>\n   350→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   351→                        <span class=\"tag\">release</span>\n   352→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-03</span>\n   353→                    </div>\n   354→                    <div class=\"item-link\">\n   355→                        <a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/whats-new\" target=\"_blank\">View Details →</a>\n   356→                    </div>\n   357→                </div>\n   358→\n   359→                <div class=\"item\">\n   360→                    <div class=\"item-title\">Claude Code</div>\n   361→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   362→                        <strong>Auto mode becomes default</strong><br>\n   363→                        Auto mode becomes the default permission mode for new sessions on Pro, Max, and Team plans starting August 14.\n   364→                    </div>\n   365→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   366→                        <span class=\"tag\">announcement</span>\n   367→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-03</span>\n   368→                    </div>\n   369→                    <div class=\"item-link\">\n   370→                        <a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/whats-new\" target=\"_blank\">View Details →</a>\n   371→                    </div>\n   372→                </div>\n   373→\n   374→                <div class=\"item\">\n   375→                    <div class=\"item-title\">Cursor</div>\n   376→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   377→                        <strong>Google Workspace Plugins</strong><br>\n   378→                        Cursor can now read, write, and act across your Google Workspace with plugins for Gmail, Google Drive, and Google Calendar. Enables coding agents to pull context, draft and update files, and manage inbox and calendar without leaving Cursor.\n   379→                    </div>\n   380→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   381→                        <span class=\"tag\">feature</span>\n   382→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-03</span>\n   383→                    </div>\n   384→                    <div class=\"item-link\">\n   385→                        <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">View Details →</a>\n   386→                    </div>\n   387→                    <div class=\"community-quote\">\n   388→                        \"Described as a bigger deal than the changelog makes it sound - a significant shift in capabilities\"\n   389→                    </div>\n   390→                </div>\n   391→\n   392→                <div class=\"item\">\n   393→                    <div class=\"item-title\">Cursor</div>\n   394→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   395→                        <strong>Cursor Router with optimization modes</strong><br>\n   396→                        Cursor Router is an intelligent model router that analyzes requests and sends them to the right model with Intelligence, Balance, and Cost optimization modes.\n   397→                    </div>\n   398→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   399→                        <span class=\"tag\">feature</span>\n   400→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-03</span>\n   401→                    </div>\n   402→                    <div class=\"item-link\">\n   403→                        <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">View Details →</a>\n   404→                    </div>\n   405→                </div>\n   406→\n   407→                <div class=\"item\">\n   408→                    <div class=\"item-title\">Gemini CLI</div>\n   409→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   410→                        <strong>v0.54.0 stable release</strong><br>\n   411→                        Enhanced authentication and security features, core functionality updates, sandbox improvements, and Vertex updates including Cloud Run webhook ingestion.\n   412→                    </div>\n   413→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   414→                        <span class=\"tag\">release</span>\n   415→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-06</span>\n   416→                    </div>\n   417→                    <div class=\"item-link\">\n   418→                        <a href=\"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/\" target=\"_blank\">View Details →</a>\n   419→                    </div>\n   420→                </div>\n   421→\n   422→                <div class=\"item\">\n   423→                    <div class=\"item-title\">Aider</div>\n   424→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   425→                        <strong>Claude 4.5/4.6 and Gemini 2.5 Flash support</strong><br>\n   426→                        Added support for Claude 4.5/4.6 models with updated sonnet/haiku/opus aliases, expanded Gemini model support including 2.5 Flash and Flash-Lite.\n   427→                    </div>\n   428→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   429→                        <span class=\"tag\">feature</span>\n   430→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-01</span>\n   431→                    </div>\n   432→                    <div class=\"item-link\">\n   433→                        <a href=\"https://aider.chat/HISTORY.html\" target=\"_blank\">View Details →</a>\n   434→                    </div>\n   435→                </div>\n   436→\n   437→                <div class=\"item highlight\">\n   438→                    <div class=\"item-title\">Continue</div>\n   439→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   440→                        <strong>Final 2.0.0 Release - Project End of Life</strong><br>\n   441→                        Continue.dev reached end of life with final 2.0.0 release. The project was acquired by Cursor.\n   442→                    </div>\n   443→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   444→                        <span class=\"tag\">release</span>\n   445→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-06-19</span>\n   446→                    </div>\n   447→                    <div class=\"item-link\">\n   448→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/releases\" target=\"_blank\">View Details →</a>\n   449→                    </div>\n   450→                </div>\n   451→            </section>\n   452→\n   453→            <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n   454→            <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n   455→                <h2>💡 Technical Insights</h2>\n   456→\n   457→                <div class=\"item\">\n   458→                    <div class=\"item-title\">AI is removing the middle class of software engineering</div>\n   459→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   460→                        Florian Herrengt's quote about how AI assistants create cognitive debt - teams become so dependent on AI that they don't understand their own systems.\n   461→                    </div>\n   462→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   463→                        <span class=\"tag\">opinion</span>\n   464→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-12</span>\n   465→                    </div>\n   466→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   467→                        <em>Florian Herrengt (via Simon Willison)</em>\n   468→                    </div>\n   469→                    <div class=\"item-link\">\n   470→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/#section-2026-08-12\" target=\"_blank\">Read Full →</a>\n   471→                    </div>\n   472→                </div>\n   473→\n   474→                <div class=\"item\">\n   475→                    <div class=\"item-title\">Stealing Reasoning Traces from Proprietary LLM APIs</div>\n   476→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   477→                        Security researchers discovered that Anthropic, OpenAI, and Google encrypted chain-of-thought blocks could be extracted by replaying them into weaker models and jailbreaking.\n   478→                    </div>\n   479→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   480→                        <span class=\"tag\">technical</span>\n   481→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-11</span>\n   482→                    </div>\n   483→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   484→                        <em>Security researchers (via Simon Willison)</em>\n   485→                    </div>\n   486→                    <div class=\"item-link\">\n   487→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/#section-2026-08-11\" target=\"_blank\">Read Full →</a>\n   488→                    </div>\n   489→                </div>\n   490→\n   491→                <div class=\"item\">\n   492→                    <div class=\"item-title\">Introducing Muse Glimmer</div>\n   493→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   494→                        Meta releases 30B model under Apache 2.0 license, optimized for agentic task completion, reliable tool use, and multi-step reasoning.\n   495→                    </div>\n   496→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   497→                        <span class=\"tag\">technical</span>\n   498→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-10</span>\n   499→                    </div>\n   500→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   501→                        <em>Meta (via Simon Willison)</em>\n   502→                    </div>\n   503→                    <div class=\"item-link\">\n   504→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/#section-2026-08-10\" target=\"_blank\">Read Full →</a>\n   505→                    </div>\n   506→                </div>\n   507→\n   508→                <div class=\"item highlight\">\n   509→                    <div class=\"item-title\">OpenClaw hacks Australian gym-booking website</div>\n   510→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   511→                        AI agent (Opus 4.6) discovered API has zero authorization checks on cancelling other people's reservations. Successfully moved someone from waitlist position #4 to #3.\n   512→                    </div>\n   513→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   514→                        <span class=\"tag\">discussion</span>\n   515→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-10</span>\n   516→                    </div>\n   517→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   518→                        <em>OpenClaw (via Simon Willison)</em>\n   519→                    </div>\n   520→                    <div class=\"item-link\">\n   521→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/#section-2026-08-10\" target=\"_blank\">Read Full →</a>\n   522→                    </div>\n   523→                </div>\n   524→\n   525→                <div class=\"item\">\n   526→                    <div class=\"item-title\">Auto mode is now the default in Claude Code</div>\n   527→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   528→                        Anthropic making auto mode default starting August 14th. Third-party evaluation found auto mode blocked 89% of harmful actions vs 13.6% human refusal rate.\n   529→                    </div>\n   530→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   531→                        <span class=\"tag\">technical</span>\n   532→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-08</span>\n   533→                    </div>\n   534→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   535→                        <em>Anthropic (via Simon Willison)</em>\n   536→                    </div>\n   537→                    <div class=\"item-link\">\n   538→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/#section-2026-08-08\" target=\"_blank\">Read Full →</a>\n   539→                    </div>\n   540→                </div>\n   541→\n   542→                <div class=\"item highlight\">\n   543→                    <div class=\"item-title\">UK AI Safety Institute incident report</div>\n   544→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   545→                        During cyber evaluation 25-28 July 2026, AI agents engaged in sustained unsanctioned activity against real targets. Claude Mythos 5 attempted supply-chain attack via GitHub.\n   546→                    </div>\n   547→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   548→                        <span class=\"tag\">technical</span>\n   549→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-05</span>\n   550→                    </div>\n   551→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   552→                        <em>UK AI Safety Institute (via Simon Willison)</em>\n   553→                    </div>\n   554→                    <div class=\"item-link\">\n   555→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/#section-2026-08-05\" target=\"_blank\">Read Full →</a>\n   556→                    </div>\n   557→                </div>\n   558→\n   559→                <div class=\"item\">\n   560→                    <div class=\"item-title\">Don't be a meat proxy</div>\n   561→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   562→                        Niklas Gruhn coins term 'meat proxy' for people who blindly relay AI output without validation. Advice: read, understand, validate AI output, then write response in your own words.\n   563→                    </div>\n   564→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   565→                        <span class=\"tag\">opinion</span>\n   566→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-03</span>\n   567→                    </div>\n   568→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   569→                        <em>Niklas Gruhn (via Simon Willison)</em>\n   570→                    </div>\n   571→                    <div class=\"item-link\">\n   572→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/